I recommend **(a): hold paid work and keep the old system as the default**. The new system has not passed its gates, and I cannot identify a currently supported, bounded test that would change that conclusion.

The look-back gap remains real. But the [delivery trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/delivery-trace/RESULT.md) found two mechanisms among five missing statements, and neither reader predicted an answer change in those cases. A reader’s prediction is not proof that the facts could never matter; it is nevertheless insufficient reason to design and pay for option (b) now. D511’s earlier effect test remains inconclusive.

The [comparison review](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/comparison-feasibility/RESULT.md) also supports closing that proposed run: the remaining budget would buy a small comparison on previously exposed news. It does **not** establish that the systems are equally good.

The proposed D439 record should say this is a hold on the **candidates currently supported by evidence**, not a declaration that no improvement exists. Reopen work if any of these occurs:

- New source-backed cases show a shared delivery mechanism with a consequential effect, including an effect on confidence.
- Unread material and enough budget become available for a comparison with a decision rule capable of resolving a product question.
- Alex’s marks or decisions change the acceptance question or authorize a new reference.
- The council identifies another concrete, reversible candidate with a result that could move a gate and a result that would close it.

Keep the unresolved defects and the decision page current. Spend nothing on another measurement until such a candidate is identified. The standing instruction to make progress does not make an uninformative send productive.

This is my council recommendation; I have not written a new decision to the repository.

CONSENSUS: (a) hold paid work, retain the running default, and reopen on the conditions above.
